WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.110
If you've seen the trailer for Us, Jordan
Peele's follow-up to Get Out, then you probably

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:10.440
noticed a familiar face or two in the mix
particularly the family's matriarch, Adelaide.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.100
In case you didn't know, the name of the actress
playing her is Lupita Nyong'o, and there's

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.680
good reason she looks so familiar.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.140
Like so many big screen successes before her,
Lupita Nyong'o actually got her big break

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.000
in television.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.040
After appearing in a couple of short films
such as The Roadside, she was cast in the

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.140
MTV Africa production Shuga.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:34.180
A daring and explicit series set in Kenya
and designed to promote safe sex, awareness,

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.580
and tolerance, Shuga has yet to air in the
United States.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.640
But some people in Hollywood saw it and it
turned out that was all she needed.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.400
In 2013, America was finally introduced to
Nyong'o, and it was worth the wait.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.720
Working alongside acting heavyweights like
Michael Fassbender, Chiwetel Ejiofor, and

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:57.050
Sarah Paulson, Nyong'o made her big screen
debut in 12 Years a Slave as the tragically

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.180
tormented Patsey.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.791
The performance earned raves from critics
and audiences alike, culminating in Nyong'o

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.060
taking home the Oscar for Best Supporting
Actress.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.980
After winning the oscar for 12 Years a Slave,
Nyong'o was instantly catapulted to worldwide

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:11.480
superstardom.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:16.280
But her next big role wasn't in acting at
all it was as the face of the French luxury

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.640
cosmetics and perfume company Lancôme, who
signed Nyong'o in 2014.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.120
In the years since, she's helped propel the
brand to new heights, while becoming a global

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.120
fashion icon.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.180
Unfortunately, Nyong'o's first big screen
venture after 12 Years A Slave was less than

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:32.700
memorable.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:38.800
A pulpy, action-packed thriller, 2014's Non-Stop
starred Liam Neeson as a dude with a particular

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.560
set of skills, only this time, on an airplane.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.600
It's a bombastic, often baffling piece of
work that makes little use of its talented

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.100
cast.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.979
That includes Nyong'o, whose brief turn as
a flight attendant in transit barely registers

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.520
among all the action movie bluster.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.780
Unlike many actors, Lupita Nyong'o did not
first discover her passion for performing

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.340
in theater.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.600
Instead, she bean as a production assistant
on film productions including The Constant

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.840
Gardener, where she says she learned a lot
from working with star Ralph Fiennes . That

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.940
experience convinced her to give acting a
serious go, and in 2009 she enrolled in the

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.640
Yale School of Drama, where she got her first
stage work.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.689
In 2015, she finally got the chance to take
the theater world by storm when she appeared

00:02:20.689 --> 00:02:22.420
in the Broadway play Eclipsed.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:27.520
Written by Nyong'o's future Black Panther
co-star Danai Gurira, Eclipsed made history

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:31.900
by becoming the first play to premiere on
Broadway with an all-black, all-female cast

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.169
and creative team.

00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:38.029
It also earned Nyong'o a well-deserved Tony
nomination for Best Actress, which she felt

00:02:38.029 --> 00:02:40.680
wasn't just for her, but for all women of
color.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.700
"We are being heard, we are being appreciated,
and we are being celebrated, which is really,

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.700
really amazing."

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.300
Just as its title implied, Non-Stop couldn't
stop Nyong'o's ascendance.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:57.609
At the end of 2015, she had a small but key
role in the biggest domestic box office hit

00:02:57.609 --> 00:03:00.160
in history, Star Wars: The Force Awakens.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.300
Don't remember seeing her?

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.820
That's because you didn't.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.820
Nyong'o actually did motion capture and voice
work to bring the CGI character Maz Kanata

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:12.129
to life, helping make the mysterious tavern
owner one of the more intriguing new faces

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:13.700
in the current Star Wars trilogy.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:20.780
Directed by Mira Nair and based on an article
from ESPN The Magazine, 2016's Queen of Katwe

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:25.319
tells the uplifting story of a ten-year-old
girl from a Ugandan slum whose life changes

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.820
dramatically upon discovering the game of
chess.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.240
Nyong'o is at the center of the heartwarming
drama, helping to soften the film's edges

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.520
with a warm, grounded performance as the young
girl's loving mother.

00:03:35.809 --> 00:03:40.299
Though the film wasn't a mainstream hit, it
garnered acclaim from critics, with Nyong'o

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.380
again singled out for her performance.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.820
So how does Nyong'o relax when she's not making
movies?

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.820
By becoming a music icon as well!

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.359
Considering she got her start on MTV, it makes
sense.

00:03:51.359 --> 00:03:56.183
Way back in 2009, she was actually nominated
for an MTV Africa Music Award in 2009 for

00:03:56.183 --> 00:04:00.580
directing the music video for fellow Kenyan
Wahu's song "The Little Things You Do."

00:04:00.689 --> 00:04:06.400
In 2016, she showed her love of music by appearing
opposite Regina Hall in a particularly epic

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.900
episode of Lip-Sync Battle.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:13.440
And in 2017, she starred in the music video
for "Many Faced God," a collaboration between

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.740
James Blake and hip hop mogul Jay-Z.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.180
One of the biggest films in recent memory,
both in terms of box office success and cultural

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.660
impact, was 2018's Black Panther.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.000
Many critics and fans have praised the film
for its depiction of powerful women, and at

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.740
the forefront was Nyong'o as the warrior Nakia.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:35.660
The film also represented a unique moment
in Nyong'o's career, bringing together past,

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.460
present, and future collaborators.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:42.539
Not only did she reunite with fellow Star
Wars CGI co-star Andy Serkis and her broadway

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.080
playwright Danai Gurira, it also teamed her
up with future Us co-star Winston Duke.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.199
With such talent, grace, and commitment, is
it any wonder that even superheroes are awestruck

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:52.880
in her presence?

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:53.700
"Nakia"

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:58.700
"Hi."

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.040
"did he freeze?"

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.700
"like an antelope in headlights!"

